  "description": "The 2026 election for Michigan's 5th Congressional District pits incumbent Republican Rep. Tim Walberg against Democratic challenger Christian Vukasovich. The district covers southern Michigan including Branch, Cass, Hillsdale, Jackson, Lenawee, Monroe, and St. Joseph Counties, along with portions of Berrien, Calhoun, and Kalamazoo Counties. The Cook Political Report rates the race as 'Solid R' with a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+13, reflecting the district's strong conservative lean. The primary election will be held on August 4, 2026, and the general election on November 3, 2026.",
